%erg v1
Title: Add Go unit test for nextID pure function
Created: 2026-05-05
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-05-05T08:34Z claude created

--- body ---
`tickets/tools/go/nextid.go` implements `nextID(dir string) string` — a pure
function that scans a directory for `NNNN-*.erg` filenames and returns the next
sequential 4-digit ID. It is covered by 9 shell integration cases in
`test_nextid.sh` but has no Go unit test.

`nextID` has clear boundary cases suited for a table test:
- Empty directory → "0001"
- One ticket `0001-foo.erg` → "0002"
- Gap: `0001`, `0003` present → "0004" (takes max+1, not first gap)
- Max existing `0099` → "0100"
- Non-`.erg` files ignored
- Files with non-numeric prefix ignored
- Mix of `.erg` and non-`.erg`, padded IDs

Create `tickets/tools/go/nextid_test.go` with `TestNextID` table test using
`t.TempDir()` to create fixture directories.

This follows the project's stated direction (ticket 0047): pure functions
belong in Go unit tests. `nextID` is pure (reads filesystem but output is
deterministic given inputs) and the shell tests are slow compared to what a
table test in Go can cover.
